3. THE PS4 PACKAGE AND MUPDF (AGPL-3.0)
---------------------------------------

PDF support uses MuPDF 1.24.11, Copyright (C) Artifex Software, Inc., which is
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 or (at your
option) any later version. When build/mupdf-<target>/libmupdf.a is present,
MuPDF and the libraries bundled with it are linked statically into the
program, as they are in the published PS4 package. Librarian uses the official
release unmodified (mupdf-1.24.11-source.tar.gz, SHA-256
191227b96775f6705ef7d9551187511932b519273b34535a331491cf7d98163f, checked
against third_party/mupdf on 2026-10-30); it is built by tools/build_mupdf.sh.

The package is therefore a combined work. Section 13 of the GNU GPL v3 permits
combining GPL-3.0 code with AGPL-3.0 code: Librarian's own code stays under
GPL-3.0-or-later, and the combination as a whole is conveyed under the terms
of the GNU AGPL version 3 (licenses/AGPL-3.0.txt).

Anyone who distributes the package (the .pkg, or any other build that
includes MuPDF), including an unmodified copy, must:

  * give recipients the licence texts: LICENSE (GPL-3.0),
    licenses/AGPL-3.0.txt, this NOTICE and the licenses/ folder;
  * provide the Corresponding Source of the whole package under the terms of
    section 6 of the (A)GPL, either together with the package or through a
    written offer or equivalent access at no further charge. That source is:
      - Librarian's source (this project) at the same version;
      - MuPDF 1.24.11, including its thirdparty/ folder;
      - the other components in section 4, at the versions recorded in
        third_party/PROVENANCE.json;
      - the source of the OpenOrbis modules in the package;
      - the scripts used to build and package it: Makefile,
        tools/fetch_deps.py, tools/build_mupdf.sh, tools/build.ps1,
        tools/build.sh, tools/package.py and tools/make_source_release.py;
  * keep all copyright, licence and warranty notices intact (section 2).

What the build provides for this: the package itself contains LICENSE, this
NOTICE and every licence text in its licenses/ folder (/app0/licenses on the
console). tools/build.sh also writes, next to the .pkg in
dist/<release>/: LICENSE, NOTICE, SOURCE.md (how to rebuild), licenses/,
librarian-<version>-source.tar.gz, mupdf-1.24.11-source.tar.gz (the official
archive), openorbis-modules-source.tar.gz and SHA256SUMS. Publishing those
files together with the package satisfies the source requirement above.

Section 13 of the AGPL (remote network interaction): if you modify the
program and let users interact with your modified version remotely over a
network, you must offer those users the Corresponding Source of your version.
Librarian is an application that runs on the console and is not offered as a
network service.

A build without MuPDF (no libmupdf.a: PDFs are then reported as unsupported)
contains no AGPL-licensed code and is GPL-3.0-or-later as a whole.


